From e05807169540175ec597d359c1815636ad915a52 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fernando Luiz Cola <fernando.luiz@pantacor.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 16:23:56 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] libuuu: use plain stat/mmap on non-glibc Linux

musl has a 64-bit off_t unconditionally and, since 1.2.4, no longer
declares the LFS64 names (stat64, mmap64) unless _LARGEFILE64_SOURCE is
defined -- _GNU_SOURCE stopped implying it. buffer.cpp then fails with
"aggregate 'struct stat64' has incomplete type" and "'mmap64' was not
declared in this scope".

The tree already handles this situation for macOS by mapping stat_os and
mmap64 to the plain calls, which are the large-file ones there. Extend
both conditions to Linux without __GLIBC__.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Fernando Luiz Cola <fernando.luiz@pantacor.com>
---
 libuuu/buffer.cpp | 2 +-
 libuuu/buffer.h   | 4 +++-
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libuuu/buffer.cpp b/libuuu/buffer.cpp
index 1f0c64e..aa68d5f 100644
--- a/libuuu/buffer.cpp
+++ b/libuuu/buffer.cpp
@@ -51,7 +51,7 @@
 
 #ifdef WIN32
 #define stat_os _stat64
-#elif defined(__APPLE__)
+#elif defined(__APPLE__) || (defined(__linux__) && !defined(__GLIBC__))
 #define stat_os stat
 #include "dirent.h"
 #else
diff --git a/libuuu/buffer.h b/libuuu/buffer.h
index a242698..0b1d5ad 100644
--- a/libuuu/buffer.h
+++ b/libuuu/buffer.h
@@ -50,7 +50,9 @@
 #include <unistd.h>
 #endif
 
-#ifdef __APPLE__
+/* Non-glibc Linux (musl) has a 64-bit off_t unconditionally and, since musl
+ * 1.2.4, no longer exposes the LFS64 names; the plain calls are the LFS ones. */
+#if defined(__APPLE__) || (defined(__linux__) && !defined(__GLIBC__))
 #define mmap64 mmap
 #endif
 
